<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ's Peters lowers spending in 1997/98.</title>
<headline>NZ's Peters lowers spending in 1997/98.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The extra spending plans of New Zealand's centre-right coalition government for the 1997/98 year have been reduced, Treasurer Winston Peters said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Peters said spending in the first year of the government's three year term would be NZ$250 million lower than the $1.2 billion originally planned.</p>
</text>
